    "created_at": "2022-09-14T09:54:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-14T09:54:23Z",
    "body": "I can report that Live regions (such as HTML5's `<output>`) do not handle lang properly. Typically the content of Live Regions is provided by client side scripting (so where do we post the lang attribute?). \r\nOne live region ARIA role (feed) is intended for `<article>` elements. Hypothetically, each article in a feed may have a different lang setting. Is the current spec sufficiently clear that these variations need to be communicated accurately to the accessibility tree?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
