    "created_at": "2022-09-15T13:22:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-15T13:22:12Z",
    "body": "As well as the 'inline' change of language mentioned above, there is also a problem if the textContent is in one language but the attribute is in another. For example, this kind of language switch may appear at the top of an English page:\r\n\r\n````\r\n<a href=\"myfile.es.html\" lang=\"es\" alt=\"Spanish translation\">Español</a>\r\n````\r\n\r\n(Fwiw, these issues are the reason the i18n WG recommends never to put localisable text in attributes. See https://www.w3.org/TR/international-specs/#markup_elements_attributes)\r\n\r\n ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
